From: PowOS <mats@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: a task that never went live gives its window to the desktop

A task is made (show: powos-open-task's D-Bus show, the maximize op, export-new, a full-screen window) before the app's
activity connects its consumer; only then does the task go live and take the window off the desktop. When the
activity never shows it - started while the screen is off or the phone folds (the desktop is "off" for that
moment), then covered by the desktop coming back - the task stays in fallback for good while its window is still on
the Plasma desktop, where the user goes on using it: KWin took it as a task everywhere (taskFor: no export, no
desktop ownership, its own moves cancelled before 0033), and a later consumer would pull the window out of Plasma.
Log, 2026-10-28: "desktop on screen: false", "window task 11 has KWin's title bar", "desktop on screen: true", then
only "window task 11 asked to be moved" - never "window task 11 live". Now the desktop coming on screen ends every
task that never went live ("close": the app drops its card) and the window is the desktop's like the others there.
---
diff --git a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
index d33bf7c..86b2a41 100644
--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
@@ -1203,6 +1203,20 @@ void AnlandWindowTasks::setDesktopShown(bool on)
     if (!on || !workspace()) {
         return;
     }
+    // A task that never went live (its activity never showed the window: started while the screen was off or folding
+    // - the desktop is "off" for that moment - then covered by the desktop) left its window here on the desktop, where
+    // the user now works with it. It stops being a task (the app drops its card): kept, it held the window for a task
+    // nothing shows - every show/export took it as exported, and its own move was cancelled (0033) - and a later
+    // consumer would have pulled the window out of Plasma under the user's hands (2026-10-28: "window task 11 has
+    // KWin's title bar" between "desktop on screen: false" and "true" on a fold, never "window task 11 live").
+    const auto tasks = m_tasks;
+    for (AnlandWindowTask *task : tasks) {
+        if (!task->exported()) {
+            qCInfo(KWIN_ANLAND) << "window task" << task->id() << "never went live: its window stays on the desktop";
+            send({QStringLiteral("close"), QString::number(task->id())});
+            remove(task);
+        }
+    }
     // On screen: every application window on it now is the desktop's. Leaving it ("export-new 1" again, the unfolded
     // home) must not pull them out into floating tasks: the user left them in Plasma and finds them there.
     for (Window *window : workspace()->windows()) {
diff --git a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h
index 9e29872..1d03087 100644
--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.h
@@ -72,6 +72,11 @@ public:
     {
         return m_fullScreen;
     }
+    /** Its task went live once: the window is off the desktop, on the tasks desktop (until the task goes). */
+    bool exported() const
+    {
+        return m_exported;
+    }
     /**
      * The task's size in its pixels ("size" from the app: a floating window being resized). Its buffers stay at the
      * screen's size, so the window takes the new size at once - a configure, drawn at its real size top-left when it
